    gr "I know what happened to Mom and Dad."

    "The words hit me like a ton of bricks, my hand gripping the phone tight enough for its edges to bite into my palm."

    "A deep but shaky breath brings me back to the moment."

    "(They’re gone. Grace isn’t.)"

    "(I’ll figure out what that means when she’s safe again.)"

    mcmac "Okay."

    mcmac "We’ll talk about that in a minute. Where are you?"

    gr "Outside of town."

    gr "Listen, that isn’t what’s important right now."

    mcmac "How can that not be important?"

    mcmac "You were kidnapped, Grace! I’ve spent days trying to find you, and Damien—!"

    gr "Do you know what he is?"

    "I swallow hard, my eyes settling on Mackenzie."

    "(If I out what Damien is, will that put Mac in danger? Does Grace really know?)"

    mcmac "Yeah, I do."

    gr "Then you know why I can’t come home."

    gr "Not yet."

    mcmac "Grace, we stopped Damien. He’s knocked out and in cuffs."

    "Mackenzie’s phone buzzes, and she checks it before turning the screen my way."

    "It’s a text from the deputy, confirming the 'suspect' is locked up at the station."

    "I mouth ‘can you hear this’ her way and Mackenzie nods."

    "(Thank you, werewolf senses. I don’t want Grace to flip she’s out on speakerphone.)"

    gr "Great."

    gr "They’ll be happy to hear that."

    mcmac "They? Who the hell is ‘they’?"

    gr "The people that have been explaining things to me."

    "I strain to listen over the line. In the background, I can hear movement, the rustle of footsteps and soft voices."

    "Whoever’s talking is too far away for me to understand."

    gr "Listen, I don’t even know where to start. But I got away, and I’m fine."

    gr "I’m staying here until I get all the answers, okay?"

    $menuhideborder = True
    menu macs2e1c1:
        "A. No, not okay.":
            $menuhideborder = False
            mcmac "No, it’s not okay!"
            mcmac "For all I know, some weird trucker took you off the road and forced you to make this call."
            "Grace laughs, and I’m happy to hear the sound before realising it means she’s not taking me seriously."

        "B. Where is 'here?'":
            $menuhideborder = False
            mcmac "Where is 'here'? Can you at least tell me that?"

            "There's a long pause."

            "More people are talking in the background, but I still can't make out what any of them are saying."
            gr "No, I can't. I'm sorry."
        "C. This doesn't make sense.":
            $menuhideborder = False
            mcmac "Grace, this doesn't make any sense."
            gr "I know."
            gr "It will eventually, I promise. I just…I can't explain right now."

    "Mackenzie tenses with concern next to me, offering her hand."

    "I take it in silent gratitude, needing the anchor to keep ahold of myself."

    gr "The people I’m with..."

    gr "They have resources, okay? Answers to questions I’ve had for years."

    mcmac "I get that."
    mcmac "Can’t I meet them, then? Can’t I hear those answers too?"

    "(She’s really not budging.)"

    mcmac "Everyone’s worried about you, Grace. We want you home."

    gr "Bullshit."
    "The spike of anger in Grace’s voice catches me off-guard."

    gr "Maybe you do, but the rest of the town has treated us like freaks since Mom and Dad died."
    gr "And it got worse when Grandma did too! Like they think our family’s cursed or something."

    "I remember the looks and whispers after the funeral. The only people who didn’t change were..."

    "(Everyone who just helped me fight Damien.)"

    mcmac "At least let me see you, Grace. Let’s figure this out together."

    gr "..."
    gr "I’ll be in touch soon. Don’t worry about me."

    "A loud beep in my ear ends the call. Panic races through me as I rush to call Grace back, but it goes straight to voicemail."

    mcmac "Damn it. She turned the phone off."

    mcmac "Mac, I..."

    "Tears break from the corner of my eyes and Mackenzie puts an arm around my shoulders, letting my head rest against the curve of her neck."

    "She’s warm, and I press closer, trying to feel steady again."

    ma "Grace is okay, [genericfn]."
    ma "We’ve got to find her, but she’s okay."

    "I nod, repeating the words over and over in my head."

    "Mackenzie's fingers cup my chin, tilting my head up so we’re to eye."

    ma "Let’s get you inside, alright?"

    mcmac "...Yeah."

    "Mackenzie kisses me softly in the lips, and I lean into it."

    "When she finally pulls away, the world doesn’t feel like it’s falling apart anymore."

    "(At least for now.)"

    "As soon as we’re in the house, I lock the door, pocketing my keys after checking my phone over last time."

    "There’s no new text or call, no clue as to where Grace might have been calling from."

    "I should be exhausted, but the shock burned away every bit of fatigue, leaving me with adrenaline pulling through my body."

    "(Deep breaths. Just occupy yourself.)"

    "Mackenzie unclips her radio before unbuttoning her shirt and pulling it off with a sigh of relief, rolling the kinks out of her shoulders."

    mcmac "You want some coffee or something, Mac?"
    mcmac "Or I could cook something. You’ve got to be starved after fighting Damien and..."
    mcmac "Crushing cars, which is really impressive but probably made you work up a sweat —!"
    mcmac "Laundry. We could do laundry."

    "The words are spoiling past my lips faster than I can stop them, and I choke on the next tight syllable before Mackenzie’s arms wrap around me in a tight hug."

    "For a moment, she doesn’t speak, rubbing my back until I’m breathing evenly again."

    mcmac "Mac, I’m so scared."

    ma "I know. So don’t worry about me."

    ma "Let me take care of you."

    "I manage a weak nod, only to let out a little sound of surprise when Mackenzie scoops me tight up into her arms."

    "She eases me out of my vest and pulls off my glasses before taking me over to the couch,"

    "framing her body around mine so I’m cradled between her warmth and the soft cushions."

    "Tension uncoils from my body in waves, a sense of safety filling its place."

    "It’s such a relief that I almost start crying again."

    mcmac "What can we do?"

    ma "This is going to be hard to hear, but not a lot."
    ma "Grace is eighteen. The state police won’t even take a missing persons report without proof of foul play."

    mcmac "But she was ..."
    mcmac "Shit. She got away from Damien, and you already have him in custody."
    ma "Exactly. We also got a proof of life call."
    ma "I won’t stop looking for her, [genericfn], but now it’s got to be off the books."

    mcmac "I just don’t understand who she could be with."

    ma "I don’t either. But maybe with a few days to settle, she’ll come home."

    ma "Her life just got flipped upside down. The same thing happened to you."

    "I run my fingers up and down Mackenzie’s arm, remembering where the gauze was there just a day out two ago."

    "There’s a sigh of her injuries now, barely a hint of the fight where she overwhelmed Damien."

    mcmac "It worked out pretty well on my side."

    ma "And it might on hers too. I..."
    ma "I know it’s not the same thing, but I watched three of my cousins turn legal and walk into a recruiter’s office the next week."

    ma "The kids I teased about prom just a couple months before, signed up to go to war. It scared the hell out of me."

    mcmac "What did you do?"

    ma "Nothing. They’re adults, and it’s family tradition."
    ma "I mean, the only reason I didn’t go in is because my blood ran true. Can’t exactly get away with the change in the middle of basic training."

    "Grace could have signed up for that."

    "Hell, she could have run off and gotten married, or changed her name and disappeared from Havenfall forever."

    "(I’m not used to thinking of her as an adult.)"

    $menuhideborder = True
    menu macs2e1c2:
        "A. She's still my baby sister.":
            $menuhideborder = False
            mcmac "Eighteen or not, she's still my baby sister."

            ma "And she always will be. Nothing's going to change that."

        "B. I don't have any other family.":
            $menuhideborder = False

            mcmac "I don’t have any other family, Mac. Grace is all I have left."

            ma "I know, which is why I want to get her back to you."

        "C. I'd be fine if it was the military.":
            $menuhideborder = False
            mcmac "If she was going into the military, at least I'd know where she was."
            ma "She can't have gone too far. Not in this little time."

    "(We won’t find Grace tonight. I just have to accept that.)"

    "I snuggle closer into Mac’s embrace, running over the night’s events in my head again."

    "The fact that we’re here, together and safe, is a miracle in itself."

    mcmac "I can’t believe we found each other."
    mcmac "I mean, we grew up in the same place together, but..."

    ma "No, I get it."
    ma "Makes me think of a puzzle. You slide in one missing piece and the whole thing suddenly makes sense."

    mcmac "Yeah."

    "(No wonder we fit so well together.)"

    "My eyes start to flutter closed, exhaustion pressing in on me from all sides. With Mackenzie holding me, I fall asleep."

    "In my dreams, everything is awash in moonlight."

    "A knock at the door pulls me out of a very deep sleep."
    "I’m confused about the weight next to me before I realise I’m groping at Mackenzie’s side."

    "(Whoops.)"

    "She stirs beside me, and I blush when a growl rumbles out of her throat. Green eyes open slowly, locking with mine."

    ma "Any idea who that is?"

    mcmac "No. You?"

    "Mackenzie sits up before taking in a deep breath. After she scents the air, her entire body goes rigid, teeth bared."

    mcmac "What’s wrong?"

    ma "It’s one of Damien’s wolves."
    ma "I’m going to get the door, but stay behind me, okay?"

    mcmac "I will."

    "More than anything, I want to cuddle back to sleep with her, but Mackenzie’s high on alert before reaching for the door and pulling it open."

    "The werewolf standing there raises her hands immediately, offering a weak smile."

    $sidecharone = "Werewolf"

    sid1 "Good morning."

    ma "You just made it the opposite. Why are you still in town?"

    "The forceful question is sharpened like a knife by Mackenzie’s tone, and from the way the other werewolf steps back, I think she feels the blade right at her throat."

    sid1 "I don’t have anywhere to go. I’m not a Rider."
    sid1 "You’re an alpha, but you don’t have a  pack, right? You need people."

    ma "I don’t need anything from you."

    sid1 "Please. There has to be something you want."

    "(Being without a pack must be a pretty big deal. She looks really worried about being left alone.)"

    ma "Listen..."

    "Mackenzie takes a step forward, filling the doorway."

    ma "What’s your name?"

    sid1 "Annabelle. Annabelle Sheppard."

    ma "Annabelle, if you were human, I’d have you in lockup right now for kidnapping, assault, and a dozen other charges."

    ma "The only reason you’re not behind bars with Damien right now is my holding cell isn’t built for our kind. He’s trouble enough."

    "Annabelle curls into herself a bit, shoulders tight and arms wrapping around her body."

    ann "He’ll be in more trouble pretty soon."

    ma "What’s that supposed to mean?"

    ann "Beau has to be on his way by now."

    "The name makes Mackenzie’s eyes flash gold, and that shift sends an answering ripple of adrenaline through me."

    ma "Beau? Beau Rider?"

    "(Is that Damien’s alpha? I have a bad feeling about this.)"

    ann "Yeah. The ride’s only six hours from here."
    ann "I can tell you more about him. I can tell you a lot if you—!"

    "Mackenzie’s hand moves almost faster than I can see, catching Annabelle by the jaw and pulling forward."

    "In that tight grip, her throat is bared, eyes wide as she looks up at Mackenzie."

    ma "You want protection from him?"

    ann "Everyone does."

    ma "So you think sniffing around my partner’s door is going to give you that?"

    ann "No, I..."

    ma "Listen to me."
    ma "Look for the girl you took. Grace [genericln]."
    ma "Maybe, just maybe, if you find her for me, I won’t drag you to the Illinois border and toss you to the alphas there."
    ma "How’s that sound?"

    "Annabelle nods, the fear in her eyes fading as Mackenzie lets go of her."

    ma "Get out of here."

    "She’s gone in a blur, cutting through someone else’s yard rather than daring to take the open street."

    "Mackenzie pulls the door shut, then sets the lock with a sigh."

    mcmac "You scared the hell out of her, Mac."

    "Mackenzie’s face flushed with heat, smile turning sheepish."

    ma "A lot more than I meant to, actually. The rumors must be true."

    mcmac "Rumors?"

    ma "I’ve heard one of the alphas in Chicago keeps a silver axe above her desk to deal with troublemakers."

    "(Yikes. No wonder Annabelle fled with her tail between her legs.)"
